/** "The Abacus Song": the city counting. A-flat Mixolydian (the flat seventh, G-flat), 4/4 at 112 bpm: a marimba ostinato that groups its eighths three, three and two (accents on the first of each group) while the kick plays four and four, so the two lean on each other; the intro builds it up one bead at a time; a pipa tune over it, a flute holding chord tones in the second round, a clave on the 3+3+2 and a wood block on the straight eighths, a rim click, hats and an agogo; the last round of the middle puts everything on at once. Plays with the usual layers. */
